{"book":23,"chapter":36,"context":{"chapter":36,"title":"Assyria's Envoy at the Wall","summary":"In 701 BC Sennacherib of Assyria captures Judah's fortified cities and sends his field commander to Jerusalem to mock Hezekiah's trust in Egypt and in the Lord. He shouts to the people on the wall to surrender, but they answer not a word.","background":"Chapters 36–39 closely parallel 2 Kings 18:13–20:19. Sennacherib's own annals, written on clay prisms, claim he took 46 of Hezekiah's walled cities and shut Hezekiah in Jerusalem 'like a bird in a cage,' but they do not claim he took Jerusalem. His palace reliefs of the siege of Lachish (v. 2) are now in the British Museum.","customs":[{"term":"Rabshakeh","verses":"36:2","note":"An Assyrian title, probably 'chief cupbearer,' a high official, not a personal name."},{"term":"The Syrian language","verses":"36:11","note":"Aramaic, the language of international diplomacy. Judah's officials understood it, but ordinary people on the wall did not."}],"watchFor":["'What confidence is this wherein thou trustest?' (v. 4).","He stands where Ahaz once refused to trust God (v. 2; 7:3).","The people keep silent, as the king commanded (v. 21)."],"connections":["2 Kings 18:13-37","2 Chronicles 32:9-19","Isaiah 7:3","Psalms 46:1-3"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["וַיְהִי","vayhi","H1961","Hc/Vqw3ms","and it was"],["בְּאַרְבַּע","be'arba'","H702","HR/Acbsa","in four-"],["עֶשְׂרֵה","'esreh","H6240","HAcbsa","teen"],["שָׁנָה","shanah","H8141","HNcfsa","year"],["לַמֶּלֶךְ","lamelekh","H4428","HRd/Ncmsa","of the king"],["חִזְקִיָּהוּ","chizkiyahu","H2396","HNpm","Hezekiah"],["עָלָה","'alah","H5927","HVqp3ms","he went up"],["סַנְחֵרִיב","sancheriv","H5576","HNpm","Sennacherib"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh-","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["אַשּׁוּר","'ashur","H804","HNpl","Assyria"],["עַל","'al","H5921","HR","on"],["כָּל","kol-","H3605","HNcmsc","all"],["עָרֵי","'arei","H5892","HNcmpc","[the] cities of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["הַבְּצֻר